The woff2 files are the latin variable builds published by the Fontsource
project (@fontsource-variable packages, version 5.3; all axes for Fraunces,
the weight axis for the other two), copied unchanged.
The two icons in mods/attention-picker (spinner.svg, search.svg) were made for
this project.

The pictures of the documentation (preview.png, docs/assets/preview.png, drawn
from scripts/preview/preview.svg, and docs/assets/features/*.svg) are drawings
made for this project by scripts/preview/make-pictures.mjs, with made-up data.
They inline the paths of six program icons shipped with Herdr, copied unchanged
into scripts/preview/icons/:
  - git.svg, nvim.svg, gemini.svg: Simple Icons (https://simpleicons.org),
    CC0 1.0. Git, Neovim and Gemini are their owners' trademarks.
  - shell.svg: Lucide (https://lucide.dev), ISC License, with MIT-licensed
    Feather-derived icons; full notice in scripts/preview/icons/LICENSE-Lucide.txt.
  - claude.svg, codex.svg: LobeHub icons (MIT); full notice in
    scripts/preview/icons/LICENSE-LobeHub.txt. Claude and Codex are their
    owners' trademarks. No trademark rights are granted.
Their text is drawn in the first font the renderer finds from these lists:
Geist, Inter, Segoe UI, DejaVu Sans, Liberation Sans, Arial, then any
sans-serif; and for terminal text JetBrains Mono, Menlo, Consolas, DejaVu Sans
Mono, then any monospace. Which one was used is not recorded. Segoe UI, Arial,
Menlo and Consolas are system fonts that are not bundled or distributed here,
only rendered into the PNG. A real screenshot replaces the illustration before
the repository is published (see .github/PUBLISH-CHECKLIST.md).

Copies of the mod folder: keep the "SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0" and
copyright lines at the top of main.js, logic.js and ask.js, and ship the LICENSE
file with a bundled copy (a layout that includes the mod, for example).

Development tools used outside the shipped mod (not distributed with it):
Node.js (test runner), GitHub Actions.
